Licensing map for common/bw/
============================

msieve proper is public domain. The Block Wiedemann implementation under
common/bw/ is new public-domain code plus ONE vendored LGPL-2.1+
component: gf2x (the GF(2)[x] multiplication library). The CADO lingen
files vendored earlier were REMOVED on 2026-10-24 when the independent
recursive lingen (bw_lingen_own) replaced that path; their history
stays in git. Every vendored file keeps its original copyright and
license header untouched.

Provenance pins (snapshot taken 2026-10-24 via `git archive`, so the
dirty state of the live trees never leaks in):

  cado-nfs-cognition   commit b5ca9c4 ("cado-nfs: latest version")
                       /media/nas/users/jacob/factor/cado-nfs-cognition
  msieve_nfsathome     commit 0f25603 + local filter_lpbound patch
                       (re-applied and committed on the block-wiedemann
                       branch)
  cuda-mpqs            v1.0.8 (Heinrichs & Januszewski), DESIGN REFERENCE
                       ONLY - zero files copied (LGPL-3.0-only). The
                       patterns credited to it are listed in BW.md
                       ("Adopted patterns").

Directory map
-------------

  bw.h, bw.c, bw_matrix.*, bw_gpu.*, bw_krylov.c, bw_mksol.c,
  bw_checkpoint.*, bw_seq.h, bw_lingen.h, bw_lingen.cpp (dispatcher),
  bw_lingen_quad.* (standalone quadratic GPU BM + shared select/
  basecase/emit glue), bw_lingen_own.cpp (independent recursive
  lingen: own invariants, GPU basecase, gf2x arithmetic),
  bw_kernel.cu, bw_selftest.c
        New code written for this project. Public domain, same terms
        as the rest of msieve. The recursive lingen follows the
        published divide-and-conquer block-BM structure (Thome); all
        code here was written from scratch for this tree.

                       cado-nfs-cognition b5ca9c4 linalg/bwc/lingen_*,
                       tree_stats.hpp. LGPL-2.1+ (cado-nfs license).
                       Edits are local and marked with `/* bw-local */`
                       comments where they occur.

                       the level sources the lingen base case calls),
                       vendored from b5ca9c4 linalg/bblas/. LGPL-2.1+.

                       (b5ca9c4 root, generated header archived as-is).
                       LGPL-2.1+.

                       misc, omp_proxy, runtime_numeric_cast, memory,
                       getprime, sha1, portability from b5ca9c4 utils/.
                       params.hpp is replaced by a stub (the original
                       drags in the verbose/version_info layer this port
                       does not compile). LGPL-2.1+.
                       cado/utils/embedded/ is the {fmt} core
                       (MIT licensed, upstream fmtlib/fmt) as bundled
                       by cado; see cado/utils/embedded/LICENSE if
                       present, else
                       https://github.com/fmtlib/fmt/blob/master/LICENSE.

                       cado.h, select_mpi.h, lingen_fft_select.hpp,
                       memusage.h and the other compile-time stand-ins
                       that replace cado's build system.

  bw_lingen_test.c     NEW, public domain: random-recurrence validation
                       of the ported lingen (polynomial identity
                       A(x)*F(x) = 0 on the interior window).

  gf2x/                The gf2x library vendored from b5ca9c4 gf2x/
                       (upstream https://gforge.inria.fr/projects/gf2x/
                       -> https://gitlab.inria.fr/gf2x/gf2x, a mirror
                       of the copy shipped inside cado-nfs).
                       LGPL-2.1+ by default: we build with
                       toom-gpl-placeholder.c instead of toom-gpl.c, so
                       the resulting libgf2x.a avoids the GPL-3.0-only
                       Toom code. Setting BW_GPL_GF2X=1 at build time
                       swaps the real (faster) GPL Toom code in.

Static-linking note (LGPL v2.1 section 6): libmsieve.a with BW=1 is a
static combination. We satisfy the relinking requirement by shipping
the object files and the vendored sources alongside the binary (this
tree), so a user can relink a modified LGPL component. For binary-only
distribution build with BW=1 and prefer producing libmsieve_bw.so and
dynamically linking the gf2x portion; the Makefile keeps both
options open.

cuda-mpqs (LGPL-3.0-only) was studied for design patterns only; no
code, no verbatim comments, no copied identifiers. Patterns credited
to it in BW.md: circular-history backtracking in mksol, golden-hash
verification cascade, EOF completeness sentinel, strict option
validation/occupancy preflights. All code here implementing those
ideas was written from scratch.
